# Tortoise blog admin SPA — environment
# Copy to .env for local dev. Same Supabase project as the site
# (the blog_posts / blog_admins tables + blog-images bucket live there).

# Supabase project ORIGIN (see website/functions/blog/_lib.ts for the project ref).
# The browser uses it ONLY to build public Storage URLs (`getPublicUrl`) and to
# identify the objects `deleteBlogImage` may remove. It is NOT the data path and
# NOT a credential: every `rest/v1` + `storage/v1` request is rewritten to the
# same-origin `/api/sb/*` Token Handler, which attaches the server-minted Supabase
# access token. The anon key is no longer a browser requirement (#4178).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://ybetwichurajbfswfeqa.supabase.co

# The session gate is the HttpOnly `__Host-session`, read via `/api/session`; the
# data layer rides the same-origin BFF proxy (`/api/sb/*`) with that session.
# No service-role keys client-side.
